.TH "GLIB-COMPILE-RESO" 1 "" "GIO" "glib-compile-schemas"
.SH NAME
glib-compile-resources \- GLib resource compiler
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.ad l
.hy 0
.HP 23
\fBglib\-compile\-resources\fR [OPTION...] {FILE}
.ad
.hy

.SH "DESCRIPTION"

.PP
\fBglib\-compile\-resources\fR reads the resource description from \fIFILE\fR and the files that it references and creates a binary resource bundle that is suitable for use with the \fBGResource\fR API\&. The resulting bundle is then written out as\-is, or as C source for linking into an application\&.

.PP
The XML resource files normally have the filename extension \fI\&.gresource\&.xml\fR\&. For a detailed description of the XML file format, see the \fBGResource\fR documentation\&.

.SH "OPTIONS"

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help and exit

.TP
\fB\-\-target=\fITARGET\fR\fR
Store the compiled resources in the file \fITARGET\fR\&. If not specified a filename based on the \fIFILE\fR basename is used\&.

.TP
\fB\-\-sourcedir=\fIDIRECTORY\fR\fR
The files referenced in \fIFILE\fR are loaded from this directory\&. If not specified, the current directory is used\&.

.TP
\fB\-\-generate\fR
Write the output file in the format selected for by its filename extension: 

.RS

.TP
\&.c
C source

.TP
\&.h
C header

.TP
\&.gresource
resource bundle

.RE
.IP
 

.TP
\fB\-\-generate\-source\fR
Instead of a writing the resource bundle in binary form create a C source file that contains the resource bundle\&. This can then be compiled into an application for easy access\&.

.TP
\fB\-\-generate\-header\fR
Generate a header file for use with C code generated by \fB\-\-generate\-source\fR\&.

.TP
\fB\-\-generate\-dependencies\fR
Prints the list of files that the resource bundle references to standard output\&. This can be used to track dependencies in the build system\&. For example, the following make rule would mark \fItest\&.gresource\fR as depending on all the files that \fItest\&.gresource\&.xml\fR includes, so that is is automatically rebuilt if any of them change: 

.nf

test\&.gresource: test\&.gresource\&.xml $(shell $(GLIB_COMPILE_RESOURCES) \-\-generate\-dependencies test\&.gresource\&.xml)

.fi
 Note that this may or may not be portable to non\-GNU \fBmake\fR\&.

.TP
\fB\-\-c\-name\fR
Specify the prefix used for the C identifiers in the code generated by \fB\-\-generate\-source\fR and \fB\-\-generate\-header\fR\&.

.TP
\fB\-\-manual\-register\fR
By default code generated by \fB\-\-generate\-source\fR uses automatic initialization of the resource\&. This works on most systems by using the compiler support for constructors\&. However, some (uncommon) compilers may not support this, you can then specify \fB\-\-manual\-register\fR, which will generate custom register and unregister functions that your code can manually call at initialization and uninitialization time\&.

.TP
\fB\-\-internal\fR
By default code generated by \fB\-\-generate\-source\fR declares all initialization functions as \fBextern\fR\&. So they are exported unless this is prevented by a link script or other means\&. Since libraries usually want to use the functions only internally it can be more useful to declare them as G_GNUC_INTERNAL which is what \fB\-\-internal\fR does\&.

.SH "ENVIRONMENT"

.TP
\fBXMLLINT\fR
The full path to the xmllint executable\&. This is used to preprocess resources with the xml\-stripblanks preprocessing option\&. If this environment variable is not set, xmllint is searched in the \fBPATH\fR\&.

.TP
\fBGDK_PIXBUF_PIXDATA\fR
The full path to the gdk\-pixbuf\-pixdata executable\&. This is used to preprocess resources with the to\-pixdata preprocessing option\&. If this environment variable is not set, gdk\-pixbuf\-pixdata is searched in the \fBPATH\fR\&.

.SH AUTHOR
Alexander Larsson.
